                        "entry_id": "c1f1ff36-c843-3910-ba74-6aea2537f695",
                        "glosses": [
                            "делать проще, уменьшать сложность"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c6ccf30e-d059-347c-b858-1609c390d9c9",
                        "entry_id": "c1f1ff36-c843-3910-ba74-6aea2537f695",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неодобр. делать чересчур простым, примитивным, представлять в обеднённом, искажённом виде, проще, чем есть на самом деле"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae4385dc-390a-4c59-bac7-5cd47c2c56ec",
                        "source_entry_id": "c1f1ff36-c843-3910-ba74-6aea2537f695",
                        "target_lang_word": "simplify",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "simplify",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fc12710-79e7-3045-bfcd-358bda4a285b",
                                        "entry_id": "6f4d6b56-6f89-3825-b95e-e33fede65c4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make simpler, either by reducing in complexity, reducing to component parts, or making easier to understand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50d9ba15-bfbe-407f-a415-4828d07c5873",
                                                "sense_id": "9fc12710-79e7-3045-bfcd-358bda4a285b",
                                                "text": "In ancient times there existed in the region of the Tung-chia River 佟佳江 in present Liaoning a people called Kao-chü-li 高句驪. In the fifth century they moved their capital to P’ing-jang. The name of the country was simplified to Kao-li 高麗 (Korea)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2015e0cd-f8ce-404b-8c74-7b6d02271305",
                                                "sense_id": "9fc12710-79e7-3045-bfcd-358bda4a285b",
                                                "text": "Quizzed on simplifying fares, Heaton-Harris said the Government had inherited a \"mix of ticketing and unbelievable, interesting fares up and down the system, and we do want to simplify them\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "852be95e-4f3f-3f93-829c-d052e0d19181",
                                        "entry_id": "6f4d6b56-6f89-3825-b95e-e33fede65c4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become simpler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63135bdc-3177-4120-84b7-f7ea30e942bd",
                                                "sense_id": "852be95e-4f3f-3f93-829c-d052e0d19181",
                                                "text": "Thus, throughout the nineteenth century, linguists generally held that more grammatically complex languages were older and that languages tended to simplify over time—the four grammatical cases of German as contrasted with the seven of Latin, for example."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "97489013-1317-4503-b371-7ead7cf57b6e",
                        "source_entry_id": "c1f1ff36-c843-3910-ba74-6aea2537f695",
                        "target_lang_word": "facilitate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "facilitate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "075ec04b-6f3f-3108-b644-8e199af1f9b1",
                                        "entry_id": "7b2cc53a-8c9c-3bb4-af35-ee75a2ac92e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make easy or easier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a247fda-af67-4aa4-bf0f-46e2fca87065",
                                                "sense_id": "075ec04b-6f3f-3108-b644-8e199af1f9b1",
                                                "text": "Features such as trackless doors, mercury-type door interlocks, roof-mounted door fault indicator lights, rubber window glazing, improved retractable shoegear and a modified electro-pneumatic brake system designed to facilitate maintenance and improve reliability, which have proved their worth on the prototype trains, are continued in the new stock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5ac5a86-294b-4fc3-9b76-2bf59046fe8a",
                                                "sense_id": "075ec04b-6f3f-3108-b644-8e199af1f9b1",
                                                "text": "The flatness of the landscape facilitates views right across the Firth of Forth to Fife, before the railway begins to pierce the Edinburgh suburbs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2bfab92e-07ba-3211-ba4f-d50f11d2a046",
                                        "entry_id": "7b2cc53a-8c9c-3bb4-af35-ee75a2ac92e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To help bring about."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a200b88-c136-4a49-93cf-264f5c717631",
                                                "sense_id": "2bfab92e-07ba-3211-ba4f-d50f11d2a046",
                                                "text": "But while she was pursuing this thought the good genius of Sophia, or that which presided over the integrity of Mrs Honour, or perhaps mere chance, sent an accident in her way, which at once preserved her fidelity, and even facilitated the intended business."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94cc4da2-9de0-412a-9a3c-348f6c844fe2",
                                                "sense_id": "2bfab92e-07ba-3211-ba4f-d50f11d2a046",
                                                "text": "Last week, the Justice Department said it would comply with a federal judge’s order to “facilitate” the return of O.C.G., a gay man who was sent to Mexico this year despite having told American authorities that he had experienced violence there and was afraid to go back."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d790b48b-5fa6-3a68-8425-f549c06f6df1",
                                        "entry_id": "7b2cc53a-8c9c-3bb4-af35-ee75a2ac92e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To preside over (a meeting, a seminar)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
